  "conclusion": "The top 10% densest cells alone hold 79.63% of citywide population; the top 30% hold 99.56%. Istanbul's population is heavily concentrated in a minority of cells by area/count, while most grid cells (by simple count) are low-density periphery -- this is the primary, quantified explanation for why a small % of CELLS having complete access corresponds to a much larger % of POPULATION having it. This is a property of the city's population distribution, not an artifact of the accessibility model, and is independently corroborated by the V2 typology cross-reference (the two dense/transit-rich clusters hold the large majority of population and complete-access share)."
